WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.090
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.360 --> 01:34.880
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.240 --> 01:37.830
[Episode 13]

4
01:38.280 --> 01:39.070
Shēng.

5
01:39.759 --> 01:40.360
Very good.

6
01:42.200 --> 01:44.050
Child, how do you read this character?

7
01:44.050 --> 01:45.020
Yǒu.

8
01:45.560 --> 01:46.509
And this one?

9
01:47.000 --> 01:47.710
Hé.

10
01:47.789 --> 01:49.150
Good, very good.

11
01:49.750 --> 01:52.620
[Mao Zedong, Chairman of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

12
01:49.920 --> 01:51.920
Can you write this character for me?

13
01:52.350 --> 01:53.120
Okay.

14
01:54.039 --> 01:55.640
Your handwriting is so good.

15
01:58.710 --> 02:01.310
[Wei Yueqiao, Staff of the 2nd Bureau, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

16
01:59.070 --> 01:59.789
Shēng.

17
01:59.890 --> 02:01.000
Shēng. Shēng.

18
02:02.040 --> 02:02.790
Kids,

19
02:03.000 --> 02:05.280
let's start writing these characters now, okay?

20
02:05.280 --> 02:06.680
I'll check them when I get back.

21
02:06.680 --> 02:08.430
Okay, okay.

22
02:13.750 --> 02:14.950
Hello, Chairman Mao.

23
02:15.840 --> 02:16.700
Young teacher,

24
02:16.750 --> 02:19.520
you brought the Lenin Primary School to Liping?

25
02:20.000 --> 02:21.400
We've been marching and fighting all the way.

26
02:21.400 --> 02:22.560
We can finally get a rest,

27
02:22.560 --> 02:23.890
so I found a blackboard.

28
02:24.190 --> 02:25.850
The children here can't read,

29
02:26.030 --> 02:27.520
so I can't teach them texts.

30
02:27.520 --> 02:29.850
I thought I'd teach them a few characters.

31
02:30.240 --> 02:31.440
These few characters

32
02:31.590 --> 02:32.630
are seeds.

33
02:33.400 --> 02:36.150
The seeds you planted in these children's hearts

34
02:36.430 --> 02:37.840
will take root and sprout,

35
02:37.840 --> 02:39.840
and grow into a forest in the future.

36
02:40.079 --> 02:42.030
Young teacher, you are amazing.

37
02:42.680 --> 02:43.310
Thank you for your hard work.

38
02:43.310 --> 02:45.310
Thank you for your encouragement, Chairman.

39
02:45.310 --> 02:47.110
The road is full of flames of war,

40
02:47.360 --> 02:49.560
but the heart is like a spring breeze and rain.

41
02:49.560 --> 02:51.130
Actually, what I want to do most

42
02:51.130 --> 02:52.410
is this job.

43
02:55.180 --> 02:56.060
Yes, sir.

44
03:01.030 --> 03:02.890
Kids, have you finished writing?

45
03:03.080 --> 03:04.120
Finished.

46
03:04.560 --> 03:05.690
Read after me again.

47
03:05.840 --> 03:06.520
Tián.

48
03:06.870 --> 03:07.800
Tián.

49
03:08.240 --> 03:08.870
Yǒu.

50
03:09.360 --> 03:10.280
Yǒu.

51
03:10.840 --> 03:11.520
Hé.

52
03:11.910 --> 03:13.030
Hé.

53
03:13.710 --> 03:14.280
Dòu.

54
03:14.870 --> 03:15.630
Dòu.

55
03:16.120 --> 03:16.710
Huā.

56
03:17.280 --> 03:18.240
Huā.

57
03:19.000 --> 03:19.680
Shēng.

58
03:31.470 --> 03:33.870
Stop running! Stop running! Stop running!

59
03:34.190 --> 03:35.250
Where do you think you're going?

60
03:35.250 --> 03:36.440
You, don't run!

61
03:37.800 --> 03:39.730
Who told you to go fish in the river?

62
03:40.400 --> 03:41.190
I'll tan your hide!

63
03:41.190 --> 03:42.450
I'll beat you to death.

64
03:43.630 --> 03:44.680
Let's go home.

65
03:46.030 --> 03:47.870
You're down by the river every single day!

66
03:47.870 --> 03:48.910
Look at you two,

67
03:49.240 --> 03:50.700
covered head to toe in mud!

68
05:22.800 --> 05:24.310
Mrs He, take a rest.

69
05:24.720 --> 05:25.600
I'm not tired.

70
05:26.040 --> 05:26.950
Not yet?

71
05:27.240 --> 05:28.600
You've been busy all day

72
05:28.800 --> 05:30.360
and haven't even had dinner.

73
05:30.360 --> 05:31.560
You did all the physical work.

74
05:31.560 --> 05:33.190
I just sorted out some documents.

75
05:33.190 --> 05:34.070
How hard can that be?

76
05:34.070 --> 05:36.040
There are so many documents, and they're all in a mess.

77
05:36.040 --> 05:37.720
Just looking at them gives me a headache.

78
05:37.720 --> 05:38.430
I'd

79
05:38.520 --> 05:40.870
[He Zizhen, Mao Zedong's wife]

80
05:38.560 --> 05:40.760
rather wash gauze or carry stretchers.

81
05:41.040 --> 05:42.159
You think it's messy,

82
05:42.159 --> 05:43.830
but Mrs He used to be

83
05:43.830 --> 05:47.360
the confidential secretary of the Soviet Central Government.

84
05:47.950 --> 05:50.350
These documents are a piece of cake for her.

85
05:51.560 --> 05:52.560
Look at how you praise me.

86
05:52.560 --> 05:54.760
My eyes don't even feel blurry anymore.

87
06:19.040 --> 06:19.450
Greetings, Chairman.

88
06:19.450 --> 06:20.710
Greetings, Chairman.

89
06:48.930 --> 06:51.590
Are you just going to stand there and not come in?

90
07:13.430 --> 07:14.890
I'll take you out for a walk

91
07:15.310 --> 07:17.240
to experience the everyday life

92
07:17.510 --> 07:18.950
of Liping.

93
07:19.800 --> 07:21.010
I don't want to see it.

94
07:23.560 --> 07:25.290
Come and sit with me for a while.

95
08:15.480 --> 08:16.510
Maomao is here?

96
08:16.870 --> 08:17.290
Zizhen.

97
08:17.290 --> 08:17.760
Maomao.

98
08:17.790 --> 08:19.520
Zizhen, Zizhen.

99
08:20.710 --> 08:21.840
Those are cowbells.

100
08:22.920 --> 08:24.480
I heard them too just now.

101
08:29.900 --> 08:30.740
Take a seat.

102
09:27.000 --> 09:34.820
[Outskirts of Liping, Guizhou]

103
09:47.790 --> 09:49.810
Sanzhu, stop smashing it!

104
09:50.600 --> 09:51.270
Enough!

105
09:51.270 --> 09:52.530
I just want to smash it!

106
09:53.030 --> 09:54.090
Many comrades died

107
09:54.440 --> 09:56.080
protecting this thing!

108
09:56.440 --> 09:58.170
When crossing the Xiang River,

109
09:58.240 --> 10:00.440
if our company commander had taken just a few more steps,

110
10:00.440 --> 10:02.080
he'd still be alive.

111
10:02.930 --> 10:04.500
Stop smashing it!

112
10:06.210 --> 10:07.850
You won't let me smash it?

113
10:12.180 --> 10:13.570
Do you see clearly?

114
10:13.840 --> 10:16.510
This is our company commander's blood.

115
10:19.280 --> 10:20.390
Can you all see it?

116
10:21.900 --> 10:23.960
It's our company commander's blood!

117
10:41.330 --> 10:42.720
Stop playing your flute.

118
10:42.720 --> 10:44.240
Gou Yazi, where is my pot?

119
10:44.510 --> 10:45.320
I gave it away.

120
10:45.550 --> 10:46.150
You...

121
10:46.320 --> 10:47.360
Higher-ups ordered

122
10:47.360 --> 10:49.240
every company to get rid of unnecessary heavy gear.

123
10:49.240 --> 10:51.700
That big iron pot of yours is thick and heavy.

124
10:52.040 --> 10:54.350
Our instructor just brought a new one,

125
10:54.370 --> 10:55.250
thin and light.

126
10:55.440 --> 10:57.480
So I cleared out your old pot.

127
10:57.600 --> 10:59.080
Who did you give it to?

128
10:59.630 --> 11:02.440
A flag-carrying herbalist doctor at the village entrance.

129
11:02.440 --> 11:03.390
I gave it to him.

130
11:03.480 --> 11:04.670
Which way did he go?

131
11:05.680 --> 11:06.950
Don't chase him.

132
11:07.030 --> 11:09.150
He's been gone long enough to eat a whole meal.

133
11:09.150 --> 11:10.240
Gou Yazi,

134
11:10.670 --> 11:12.600
who said you could give my pot away?

135
11:12.840 --> 11:14.630
What right do you have?

136
11:14.960 --> 11:16.890
Your big iron pot is dark and heavy.

137
11:17.030 --> 11:18.590
It's too heavy for you, so you always let me carry it.

138
11:18.590 --> 11:20.030
I joined this army to fight,

139
11:20.030 --> 11:21.290
not carry pots for you.

140
11:21.390 --> 11:22.930
Am I supposed to be your pot carrier?

141
11:22.930 --> 11:25.720
If I can't carry it, it slows the whole company down.

142
11:25.720 --> 11:27.390
If we fall behind,

143
11:27.630 --> 11:29.430
the whole main force slows down.

144
11:29.670 --> 11:32.270
Just because of your pot, tens of thousands of the Central Red Army...

145
11:32.270 --> 11:34.240
You mean the Central Red Army's speed

146
11:34.240 --> 11:35.600
was delayed by my pot?

147
11:36.270 --> 11:37.240
Does that make any sense?

148
11:37.240 --> 11:39.020
Why didn't you trade your flute too?

149
11:39.020 --> 11:40.620
Don't you dare! My dad left it to me.

150
11:40.620 --> 11:41.290
Now you know

151
11:41.310 --> 11:43.390
the thing left by your dad is precious!

152
11:43.390 --> 11:45.320
Then isn't my pot precious?

153
11:45.480 --> 11:47.680
That was handed down to me by my grandpa!

154
11:50.050 --> 11:51.930
What did you trade that pot for?

155
11:52.320 --> 11:53.650
Those 6 ears of corn.

156
11:58.480 --> 12:01.270
You traded my big iron pot

157
12:01.270 --> 12:02.640
for 6 ears of corn?

158
12:02.670 --> 12:04.320
Six ears of corn!

159
12:07.040 --> 12:07.910
Fine...

160
12:15.720 --> 12:16.760
Guo,

161
12:17.150 --> 12:18.360
Gou Yazi is young and reckless.

162
12:18.360 --> 12:19.410
Don't hold it against him.

163
12:19.410 --> 12:21.220
Who's holding it against him?

164
12:21.350 --> 12:22.670
You have no idea!

165
12:23.030 --> 12:26.220
That pot has been passed down in our family for 3 generations.

166
12:26.220 --> 12:27.460
My grandpa passed it to my dad,

167
12:27.460 --> 12:29.460
and my dad passed it to me.

168
12:31.760 --> 12:34.240
My son Gousheng died

169
12:35.020 --> 12:37.100
protecting that pot.

170
12:38.670 --> 12:41.160
And he just gave it away like that!

171
12:49.240 --> 12:52.150
Guo, what exactly happened to that pot?

172
12:52.440 --> 12:54.480
Your son protected it with his life?

173
12:59.150 --> 13:00.910
You know,

174
13:01.050 --> 13:03.310
before I joined the Red Army those years,

175
13:03.720 --> 13:05.780
I took my son

176
13:05.800 --> 13:08.470
to wealthy households

177
13:08.720 --> 13:10.600
to cook at weddings and funerals.

178
13:11.670 --> 13:13.960
One year, Master Bai from Ji'an County

179
13:14.060 --> 13:16.550
held his 70th birthday banquet and hired me as head chef.

180
13:16.550 --> 13:19.240
The last dish was "Blessings and Longevity".

181
13:19.550 --> 13:21.240
I sent my son Gousheng

182
13:21.380 --> 13:24.180
to carry that dish up.

183
13:24.990 --> 13:28.160
He tripped crossing the threshold.

184
13:28.480 --> 13:31.200
Master Bai flew into a rage.

185
13:31.200 --> 13:32.340
He said smashing the dish cursed his longevity.

186
13:32.340 --> 13:35.230
He wanted to smash my pot.

187
13:35.910 --> 13:37.510
My son

188
13:37.510 --> 13:38.360
couldn't let that happen.

189
13:38.360 --> 13:40.480
He knew that pot

190
13:40.950 --> 13:42.950
was our family's whole livelihood.

191
13:43.480 --> 13:46.200
Gousheng threw himself

192
13:46.390 --> 13:48.790
on top of it to shield it.

193
13:49.240 --> 13:51.090
Then they started beating him

194
13:51.120 --> 13:53.320
with hammers and sticks.

195
13:53.630 --> 13:56.840
His head was bashed to a bloody pulp.

196
13:57.270 --> 13:59.200
I carried him home.

197
13:59.720 --> 14:02.320
My wife held him

198
14:02.580 --> 14:04.540
and wiped the blood off,

199
14:05.810 --> 14:08.480
but it kept pouring out of his ear,

200
14:08.510 --> 14:10.480
no matter

201
14:11.150 --> 14:13.870
how hard we tried.

202
14:14.360 --> 14:16.270
After 3 days and nights,

203
14:17.080 --> 14:18.440
my son was gone.

204
14:18.750 --> 14:22.480
My wife grieved herself to death not long after.

205
14:39.240 --> 14:41.030
Then the Red Army came to Ji'an

206
14:41.210 --> 14:43.070
and put those landlords on trial.

207
14:43.600 --> 14:45.200
From western to southern Jiangxi,

208
14:45.200 --> 14:47.270
from the Hunan-Jiangxi Soviet to Ruijin,

209
14:47.270 --> 14:48.320
I've carried that pot

210
14:48.320 --> 14:50.240
every step of the way.

211
14:50.650 --> 14:52.900
It's like I'm carrying my son Gousheng.

212
14:53.150 --> 14:55.280
I never once scratched it or bumped it.

213
14:55.510 --> 14:58.550
But you? You just gave it away.

214
14:59.130 --> 15:00.640
For 6 ears of corn?

215
15:00.670 --> 15:03.030
And I still have to grind 'em by hand.

216
15:18.120 --> 15:18.980
And what's this new pot?

217
15:18.980 --> 15:21.550
Look how thin and flimsy it is. You call that a pot?

218
15:21.550 --> 15:23.610
It'll burn through after a few meals.

219
15:23.720 --> 15:24.960
What was mine made of?

220
15:25.170 --> 15:26.390
Have any of you in the Red Army

221
15:26.390 --> 15:28.550
ever seen a pot so solidly built?

222
15:28.840 --> 15:30.600
My grandpa forged it himself

223
15:30.720 --> 15:32.870
during the Guangxu reign.

224
15:33.200 --> 15:34.720
Wild herbs are always a little poisonous,

225
15:34.720 --> 15:36.720
but my pot could even draw out the toxins.

226
15:36.720 --> 15:38.720
He traded it for 6 ears of corn?

227
15:38.780 --> 15:40.690
Even 600 ears of corn wouldn't...

228
15:45.230 --> 15:46.060
Gou Yazi,

229
15:46.320 --> 15:48.320
didn't you say you gave it to a quack?

230
15:48.480 --> 15:49.000
I...

231
15:49.150 --> 15:50.790
I... I lied.

232
15:50.960 --> 15:52.960
Hurry, go get it back!

233
15:53.970 --> 15:55.170
Did it get scratched?

234
15:55.550 --> 15:56.880
What exactly happened?

235
15:57.080 --> 15:59.670
I saw a toothless grandma at the village gate.

236
16:00.200 --> 16:01.840
She looked just like my grandma,

237
16:01.840 --> 16:04.080
so I gave her the pot.

238
16:05.120 --> 16:06.780
She looked like your grandma?

239
16:09.670 --> 16:10.510
You're lying.

240
16:10.530 --> 16:12.930
Hurry up and return the corn to the old lady.

241
16:13.750 --> 16:14.950
I lied about that too.

242
16:15.200 --> 16:18.240
The corn was from our own company.

243
16:18.750 --> 16:21.440
Kid, when did you learn to lie like that?

244
16:21.670 --> 16:23.000
-I'll scrub your pot for you, okay? -How could you lie to me!

245
16:23.000 --> 16:24.530
I'll scrub your pot for you!

246
16:24.840 --> 16:27.150
Scrub it. Scrub it clean.

247
16:27.150 --> 16:28.880
I'll scrub it clean, I promise.

248
16:30.420 --> 16:33.230
At least we got it back. That's all that matters.

249
16:33.420 --> 16:36.280
[Zhou Enlai, CPC Central Committee Politburo Standing Committee, Vice-Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission, General Political Commissar of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

250
16:39.030 --> 16:40.030
Vice Chairman Zhou,

251
16:40.030 --> 16:41.760
let me reheat your meal for you.

252
16:42.120 --> 16:43.150
Alright.

253
16:56.150 --> 16:58.950
[Zhu De, Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission and Commander-in-Chief of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

254
17:00.320 --> 17:01.150
Enlai.

255
17:02.990 --> 17:04.250
Commander-in-Chief,

256
17:04.440 --> 17:05.099
take a look.

257
17:05.160 --> 17:06.680
This is the draft telegram: Telegram on the Military Commission's Implementation

258
17:06.680 --> 17:09.200
of the Resolution of the Political Bureau of the Central Committee.

259
17:09.200 --> 17:10.829
Any additions?

260
17:15.000 --> 17:16.530
Another all-nighter, huh?

261
17:26.819 --> 17:27.430
Enlai,

262
17:28.349 --> 17:29.480
did you show this to Li De?

263
17:29.480 --> 17:30.160
I did.

264
17:30.310 --> 17:31.200
What was his attitude?

265
17:31.200 --> 17:33.400
He said he was too sick to even look at it.

266
17:33.510 --> 17:34.310
Later he added

267
17:34.790 --> 17:36.770
he disagreed with the Politburo's decision anyway,

268
17:36.770 --> 17:38.700
and told us to handle it ourselves.

269
17:39.710 --> 17:40.970
Then we'll ignore him.

270
17:41.700 --> 17:42.720
Here's our decision:

271
17:42.720 --> 17:44.710
the 1st and 9th Red Army Corps will form the right column;

272
17:44.710 --> 17:46.010
the 3rd and 5th Red Army Corps' Military Commission Column

273
17:46.010 --> 17:47.860
will form the left column.

274
17:48.680 --> 17:50.480
We'll advance toward northwestern Guizhou,

275
17:50.480 --> 17:52.610
reaching Jianhe, Taigong, and Gedong

276
17:53.000 --> 17:55.680
by roughly the 23rd.

277
17:55.870 --> 17:57.130
By the end of December,

278
17:57.240 --> 17:59.200
the right column will seize Shibing,

279
17:59.200 --> 18:01.240
and the left column will occupy Huangping.

280
18:01.240 --> 18:02.550
The general principle

281
18:02.550 --> 18:05.270
is to seize the initiative and destroy the Guizhou Army first.

282
18:05.270 --> 18:07.240
Since the 2nd and 6th Red Army Corps

283
18:07.240 --> 18:09.170
have already taken Taoyuan County

284
18:09.200 --> 18:11.890
and surrounded Changde,

285
18:12.530 --> 18:15.130
we'll telegraph Comrades He Long and Ren Bishi

286
18:15.560 --> 18:18.030
to keep operating actively around Changde

287
18:18.060 --> 18:19.590
and pin down the Hunan Army.

288
18:20.350 --> 18:23.130
Past Changde, across the Yuan River, is Changsha.

289
18:23.130 --> 18:25.530
He Jian will never dare take that risk.

290
18:26.440 --> 18:28.170
The moment he pulls troops back to reinforce,

291
18:28.170 --> 18:31.650
the 2nd and 6th Red Army Corps can immediately push west to Yongshun,

292
18:31.650 --> 18:34.330
tying down Xue Yue's forces in Tongren

293
18:34.360 --> 18:36.880
and the Guizhou Army in Yinjiang and Sinan.

294
18:37.330 --> 18:40.790
That'll take pressure off our advance into northern Guizhou.

295
18:41.780 --> 18:42.610
At the same time,

296
18:42.610 --> 18:44.550
we should telegraph the 4th Front Army

297
18:44.550 --> 18:46.310
to resume their offensive.

298
18:46.590 --> 18:49.960
That way, when we move into the Sichuan-Guizhou border region,

299
18:49.960 --> 18:52.490
they can pin down the Sichuan Army trying to enter Guizhou.

300
18:52.490 --> 18:53.200
Okay.

301
18:54.030 --> 18:56.000
I'll add these points right away,

302
18:56.590 --> 18:57.640
then consult

303
18:57.640 --> 18:59.090
the other members of the Military Commission

304
18:59.090 --> 19:01.550
and issue it to all corps as soon as possible.

305
19:02.130 --> 19:04.270
We should also have the General Political Department

306
19:04.270 --> 19:05.330
issue a directive,

307
19:05.680 --> 19:06.830
explaining the Politburo's decision

308
19:06.830 --> 19:09.440
to establish a new Soviet area

309
19:09.720 --> 19:11.300
on the Sichuan-Guizhou border

310
19:11.300 --> 19:13.560
to all frontline officers and soldiers.

311
19:13.920 --> 19:16.070
Make sure they understand it clearly,

312
19:16.640 --> 19:17.920
so they're not confused

313
19:17.920 --> 19:19.050
about our direction

314
19:19.240 --> 19:20.070
like before.

315
19:20.270 --> 19:23.270
Okay, I'll go to the General Political Department now

316
19:23.380 --> 19:24.830
and find Comrade Li Fuchun,

317
19:24.830 --> 19:27.230
have him draft the directive immediately.

318
19:27.780 --> 19:28.690
Enlai,

319
19:29.790 --> 19:30.850
send someone else.

320
19:31.000 --> 19:32.440
You need to get some sleep.

321
19:32.440 --> 19:33.640
I'd better go myself.

322
19:34.000 --> 19:36.310
I also want to drop by and see Chao.

323
19:36.590 --> 19:38.190
She's been quite ill lately.

324
19:38.530 --> 19:39.940
Enlai, no matter what,

325
19:39.970 --> 19:41.340
you have to rest.

326
19:42.210 --> 19:44.200
You'll wear yourself out at this rate.

327
19:44.200 --> 19:44.920
Don't worry.

328
19:44.920 --> 19:46.110
Once Comrade Bocheng gets back,

329
19:46.110 --> 19:47.550
things will lighten up.

330
19:57.630 --> 19:59.430
Vice Chairman Zhou, time to eat.

331
20:20.030 --> 20:21.270
Brother, come here.

332
20:30.850 --> 20:34.310
[Deng Yingchao, Secretary of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee]

333
20:38.600 --> 20:39.730
Okay, again.

334
20:43.400 --> 20:44.000
Very good.

335
20:46.590 --> 20:47.310
Again.

336
21:53.880 --> 21:54.880
It's contagious.

337
22:40.950 --> 22:43.790
Comrade He Cheng suggested today

338
22:43.810 --> 22:46.990
that I go to the newly established Recuperation Company to recover.

339
22:46.990 --> 22:48.340
I didn't object.

340
22:49.920 --> 22:52.050
You should take a good rest for a while.

341
22:52.650 --> 22:54.780
You are the one who needs rest the most.

342
22:54.940 --> 22:56.020
I'm fine.

343
22:56.830 --> 22:57.640
By the way,

344
22:57.830 --> 22:59.230
I mentioned to you before

345
22:59.830 --> 23:01.200
I wanted to resign as Secretary-General

346
23:01.200 --> 23:03.720
of the Central Bureau for health reasons.

347
23:04.070 --> 23:05.480
What did the Central Committee decide?

348
23:05.480 --> 23:06.850
I talked to Comrade Bo Gu,

349
23:06.850 --> 23:08.250
and he basically agreed.

350
23:12.360 --> 23:14.160
Then who will take over my work?

351
23:14.680 --> 23:16.540
Comrade Zedong and Comrade Luofu

352
23:16.670 --> 23:18.470
recommended Comrade Xiaoping.

353
23:18.550 --> 23:20.310
Comrade Xiaoping served as Secretary-General

354
23:20.310 --> 23:22.040
of Central Affairs back in 1928.

355
23:22.040 --> 23:24.240
He was also Director of the Propaganda Department of the Jiangxi Provincial Committee

356
23:24.240 --> 23:25.890
and chief editor of the Red Star newspaper.

357
23:25.890 --> 23:28.150
He'd be more than qualified to take over.

358
23:28.690 --> 23:29.780
I know him well.

359
23:30.200 --> 23:32.680
He's capable and enthusiastic.

360
23:32.810 --> 23:33.750
Don't worry.

361
23:38.510 --> 23:40.720
I'll go boil the medicine.

362
23:59.700 --> 24:00.620
Hello there.

363
24:01.090 --> 24:02.130
Come here.

364
24:07.350 --> 24:08.270
How old are you?

365
24:08.300 --> 24:09.170
4.

366
24:09.360 --> 24:10.810
4. And you?

367
24:11.160 --> 24:11.960
5.

368
24:12.000 --> 24:12.920
5.

369
24:13.110 --> 24:15.270
You're 5, and he's 4.

370
24:16.350 --> 24:19.810
Other Red Army soldiers don't have beards.

371
24:19.830 --> 24:21.380
Why do you?

372
24:21.910 --> 24:23.220
Guess what I do for a living.

373
24:23.220 --> 24:24.700
Are you an opera singer?

374
24:25.000 --> 24:26.130
I am an opera singer.

375
24:26.310 --> 24:28.180
Then why isn't your face red?

376
24:28.320 --> 24:29.600
Where's your big sword?

377
24:29.600 --> 24:31.040
My big sword...

378
24:32.400 --> 24:35.330
Can't you see my big sword? It's right here in my hand.

379
24:35.780 --> 24:37.160
You're Dong people, right?

380
24:37.160 --> 24:37.880
Yes.

381
24:37.880 --> 24:39.640
I can even sing your Dong songs.

382
24:39.830 --> 24:40.720
Really?

383
24:40.740 --> 24:42.630
Really. I can sing 2 songs.

384
24:47.770 --> 24:49.090
Let's sing together.

385
24:49.920 --> 24:52.310
♪ Zhong's house is like a toad ♪

386
24:52.500 --> 24:54.670
♪ With nothing at all ♪

387
24:55.110 --> 24:57.270
♪ Zhong's house is like a toad ♪

388
24:57.510 --> 24:59.680
♪ With nothing at all ♪

389
24:59.790 --> 25:02.170
♪ You follow him through hardship ♪

390
25:02.200 --> 25:04.000
♪ When will you see the light? ♪

391
25:04.290 --> 25:05.970
♪ You follow him... ♪

392
25:07.070 --> 25:08.670
Take it slow. Sing it slowly.

393
25:09.960 --> 25:12.480
♪ Zhong's house is like a toad ♪

394
25:12.680 --> 25:15.200
♪ With nothing at all ♪

395
25:15.830 --> 25:18.350
♪ Zhong's house is like a toad ♪

396
25:18.550 --> 25:21.070
♪ With nothing at all ♪

397
25:21.140 --> 25:23.790
♪ You follow him through hardship ♪

398
25:23.910 --> 25:25.800
♪ When will you see the light? ♪

399
25:25.830 --> 25:26.440
Sing.

400
25:26.640 --> 25:29.240
♪ You follow him through hardship ♪

401
25:31.200 --> 25:33.400
♪ Zhong's house is like a toad ♪

402
25:33.400 --> 25:36.000
♪ With nothing at all ♪

403
25:36.790 --> 25:39.440
♪ Zhong's house is like a toad ♪

404
25:39.550 --> 25:42.070
♪ With nothing at all ♪

405
25:46.160 --> 25:46.950
Uncle.

406
25:47.200 --> 25:49.000
Uncle, why did you stop singing?

407
25:49.160 --> 25:50.570
Let's go. Go.

408
25:53.920 --> 25:55.790
Auntie, Auntie!

409
25:56.260 --> 25:59.260
The bearded uncle isn't moving.

410
26:16.070 --> 26:18.030
He fell asleep.

411
26:18.530 --> 26:19.880
You can go play outside.

412
27:38.590 --> 27:39.650
Comrade Zhentang,

413
27:40.000 --> 27:41.400
we've come a long way already.

414
27:41.400 --> 27:42.600
You should head back.

415
27:42.790 --> 27:43.860
Chief of the General Staff,

416
27:43.860 --> 27:45.410
since you came to the 5th Red Army Corps,

417
27:45.410 --> 27:48.030
we've become comrades who've fought through life and death.

418
27:48.030 --> 27:49.270
If I don't see you a little further,

419
27:49.270 --> 27:50.590
I'll feel bad about it.

420
27:51.000 --> 27:52.540
You seem to have something on your mind.

421
27:52.540 --> 27:55.440
[Liu Bocheng, Chief of the General Staff of the Red Army and concurrently Commander of the Military Commission Column]

422
27:53.070 --> 27:53.590
I do.

423
27:54.050 --> 27:55.720
There's something I've got to get off my chest.

424
27:55.440 --> 27:57.800
[Dong Zhentang, Commander of the 5th Red Army Corps]

425
27:56.230 --> 27:58.350
When you're transferred back to headquarters,

426
27:58.350 --> 27:59.750
I have 2 joys and 1 sorrow.

427
28:00.000 --> 28:01.270
I'm all ears.

428
28:01.480 --> 28:02.480
First, of course,

429
28:02.590 --> 28:05.050
I'm glad you're going back to headquarters.

430
28:05.270 --> 28:07.160
It was unfair when you were removed

431
28:07.160 --> 28:08.720
from the Chief of the General Staff post.

432
28:08.720 --> 28:10.270
But when you came to our 5th Red Army Corps,

433
28:10.270 --> 28:11.070
it was the best thing

434
28:11.070 --> 28:12.730
that could've happened to us.

435
28:12.730 --> 28:13.590
Over these past months,

436
28:13.590 --> 28:15.600
I've learned so much about commanding troops from you.

437
28:15.600 --> 28:17.880
Comrade Zhentang, you're being modest.

438
28:18.590 --> 28:20.830
We've both learned from each other.

439
28:21.270 --> 28:23.110
These past few months with the 5th Red Army Corps

440
28:23.110 --> 28:25.640
gave me a chance to command on the front lines.

441
28:25.750 --> 28:28.000
I've seen firsthand how disciplined

442
28:28.590 --> 28:30.790
and hardworking the comrades here are.

443
28:30.830 --> 28:32.030
I've gained a lot.

444
28:32.430 --> 28:33.960
What's your second joy?

445
28:34.790 --> 28:35.850
Second, I feel like

446
28:36.090 --> 28:38.480
there's a change in the Military Commission.

447
28:38.480 --> 28:39.680
What kind of changes?

448
28:40.160 --> 28:41.240
A good one.

449
28:41.740 --> 28:44.440
We're not just blindly following the 6th Red Army Corps' old route.

450
28:44.440 --> 28:46.090
The troops are more flexible and mobile.

451
28:46.090 --> 28:47.750
Commanders at the corps level

452
28:48.030 --> 28:49.360
have more autonomy too.

453
28:50.240 --> 28:51.960
The Military Commission just issued the

454
28:51.960 --> 28:54.030
Telegram on the Military Commission's Implementation

455
28:54.030 --> 28:56.750
of the December 18th Resolution of the Politburo.

456
28:56.750 --> 28:58.350
It only sets general directions

457
28:58.350 --> 29:00.310
and principles for each corps.

458
29:00.720 --> 29:03.480
Unlike before, when every regiment's exact timing,

459
29:03.480 --> 29:05.010
strength, and destination

460
29:05.020 --> 29:06.750
were dictated down to the last detail.

461
29:06.750 --> 29:09.320
It needed to change, and it had to.

462
29:10.440 --> 29:11.830
This time, we're not taking the old road.

463
29:11.830 --> 29:14.000
We're turning into Guizhou, striking where the enemy is weak

464
29:14.000 --> 29:15.600
and catching them off guard.

465
29:15.640 --> 29:16.970
That takes real wisdom.

466
29:17.160 --> 29:17.960
I heard

467
29:18.240 --> 29:21.550
Chairman Mao has a voice in the Military Commission again?

468
29:21.780 --> 29:23.220
We're not the only ones

469
29:23.410 --> 29:25.020
who've been waiting for this day.

470
29:25.020 --> 29:25.750
That's true.

471
29:26.270 --> 29:28.830
Chief of the General Staff... my sorrow

472
29:29.460 --> 29:32.120
is that I won't get to work side by side

473
29:32.150 --> 29:33.950
with you anymore.

474
29:34.220 --> 29:35.550
You're my good brother, comrade,

475
29:35.550 --> 29:36.610
and my good friend.

476
29:36.890 --> 29:37.820
I may be leaving,

477
29:37.890 --> 29:40.050
but the 5th Red Army Corps still has plenty of veteran Party members.

478
29:40.050 --> 29:41.880
They get along well with each other.

479
29:41.880 --> 29:44.400
You can find good friends among them too.

480
29:44.920 --> 29:46.160
I wish I could.

481
29:46.590 --> 29:49.450
But sometimes, even when I want to get close to them,

482
29:49.590 --> 29:50.920
I just couldn't make it.

483
29:51.270 --> 29:53.160
It felt like there was a wall between us.

484
29:53.160 --> 29:54.420
I've thought about it,

485
29:54.680 --> 29:58.480
and I thought it was because of my background as a former KMT soldier.

486
30:04.460 --> 30:05.700
Comrade Zhentang,

487
30:06.210 --> 30:08.260
don't worry about that.

488
30:08.740 --> 30:11.020
The Red Army isn't like the KMT troops.

489
30:11.550 --> 30:12.880
We don't judge people by their class background.

490
30:12.880 --> 30:14.880
You might have read it in the newspapers.

491
30:14.880 --> 30:17.280
Your old commander, General Ji Hongchang,

492
30:17.510 --> 30:18.720
was killed by Chiang Kai-shek

493
30:18.720 --> 30:21.350
in Beiping for resisting Japan and opposing Chiang.

494
30:21.350 --> 30:22.980
He was a good comrade too.

495
30:23.310 --> 30:24.590
I heard about it.

496
30:25.110 --> 30:26.830
We will avenge General Ji Hongchang

497
30:26.830 --> 30:28.110
one day!

498
30:28.920 --> 30:30.240
There are many comrades in our army

499
30:30.240 --> 30:32.920
who were former KMT soldiers.

500
30:33.240 --> 30:34.300
Besides you and me,

501
30:34.640 --> 30:35.960
there's Comrade Ye Jianying,

502
30:35.960 --> 30:37.110
Comrade Peng Dehuai,

503
30:37.110 --> 30:38.270
Comrade Luo Binghui,

504
30:38.270 --> 30:39.330
and Comrade He Long

505
30:39.510 --> 30:41.000
were all former KMT soldiers.

506
30:41.000 --> 30:43.810
Our Commander-in-Chief even served as a brigade commander in the Yunnan Army.

507
30:43.810 --> 30:44.760
Politically speaking,

508
30:44.760 --> 30:45.560
Chairman Mao

509
30:45.600 --> 30:48.030
even served as acting propaganda minister for the Kuomintang once.

510
30:48.030 --> 30:49.620
We're all here

511
30:50.220 --> 30:51.280
for the same ideal.

512
30:51.960 --> 30:53.880
We all share one title:

513
30:54.550 --> 30:55.950
revolutionary comrade.

514
30:56.440 --> 30:58.640
Take our 5th Red Army Corps, for example.

515
30:58.640 --> 31:01.370
We joined the Red Army after the Ningdu Uprising,

516
31:01.790 --> 31:03.680
so we came to the revolution later.

517
31:03.680 --> 31:05.200
But the Central Committee and the Military Commission

518
31:05.200 --> 31:06.930
never treated us differently.

519
31:07.070 --> 31:08.350
Otherwise, they never would've given us

520
31:08.350 --> 31:11.000
the rearguard mission

521
31:11.350 --> 31:13.010
for this strategic transfer.

522
31:13.350 --> 31:14.920
And we've completed that mission

523
31:14.920 --> 31:16.580
successfully time and again.

524
31:16.720 --> 31:17.960
That proves the 5th Red Army Corps

525
31:17.960 --> 31:20.720
is worthy of

526
31:21.510 --> 31:23.680
the Central Committee and the Military Commission's trust.

527
31:23.680 --> 31:25.210
Chief of the General Staff,

528
31:26.200 --> 31:28.530
you've lifted the last weight off my mind.

529
31:30.070 --> 31:32.600
I, Dong Zhentang, have been loyal to the Party

530
31:33.350 --> 31:35.440
ever since the Ningdu Uprising. I've never wavered.

531
31:35.440 --> 31:36.900
I've long heard the story.

532
31:37.350 --> 31:40.010
In April 1932, right after you joined the Party,

533
31:40.200 --> 31:42.720
you donated all your savings, 3000 silver dollars,

534
31:42.720 --> 31:44.030
to Party funds.

535
31:44.440 --> 31:45.720
You declared you'd give everything

536
31:45.720 --> 31:46.550
to the cause,

537
31:46.750 --> 31:48.550
even your life.

538
31:49.590 --> 31:51.830
Chairman Mao himself praised you for it.

539
31:51.830 --> 31:54.360
Every man in our 5th Army Corps feels the same.

540
31:54.510 --> 31:55.920
Please tell the Central Committee

541
31:55.920 --> 31:57.920
and the Military Commission for me:

542
31:58.060 --> 31:58.880
we will be the iron rear guard

543
31:58.880 --> 32:00.640
of the Central Red Army,

544
32:01.310 --> 32:03.720
being unwavering and unbreakable.

545
32:04.000 --> 32:05.600
I will definitely convey it.

546
32:05.920 --> 32:07.030
Comrade Zhentang,

547
32:07.400 --> 32:10.000
a thousand-mile farewell must end somewhere.

548
32:10.350 --> 32:11.030
Take care.

549
32:11.510 --> 32:12.260
Take care.

550
32:27.990 --> 32:29.050
Comrade Jiaxiang,

551
32:29.270 --> 32:30.400
you must walk more.

552
32:30.640 --> 32:32.150
If you don't pass gas or stool,

553
32:32.150 --> 32:33.690
there's a risk of intestinal obstruction,

554
32:33.690 --> 32:35.400
which would be much harder to treat.

555
32:35.400 --> 32:37.070
Okay, thank you.

556
32:38.310 --> 32:40.000
Let's walk. Follow the doctor's orders.

557
32:40.000 --> 32:40.510
Let's walk.

558
32:40.510 --> 32:41.310
Okay.

559
32:41.860 --> 32:42.170
Come on.

560
32:42.170 --> 32:43.830
Chairman, I'll head back now.

561
32:44.960 --> 32:45.730
Okay.

562
32:55.280 --> 32:58.220
[Luofu (Zhang Wentian), Member of the Political Bureau Standing Committee of the CPC Central Committee; Chairman of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

563
32:56.680 --> 32:57.750
Stalin said

564
32:58.400 --> 33:01.480
that Communists are made of special material.

565
33:02.000 --> 33:03.270
That's never been truer

566
33:03.270 --> 33:04.670
than with Jiaxiang here.

567
33:04.750 --> 33:07.440
If I could pick the material,

568
33:07.610 --> 33:09.820
[Wang Jiaxiang, Vice-Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission; Director of the General Political Department of the Red Army]

569
33:07.750 --> 33:08.830
I'd choose steel.

570
33:10.000 --> 33:12.130
I'd melt all those shrapnel fragments

571
33:12.240 --> 33:13.400
in my body into it,

572
33:13.750 --> 33:16.150
so they stop causing trouble in my stomach.

573
33:16.560 --> 33:17.590
You're in so much pain,

574
33:17.590 --> 33:18.850
yet you can still joke.

575
33:19.420 --> 33:20.390
But,

576
33:21.000 --> 33:23.510
our bodies are gifts from our parents.

577
33:23.960 --> 33:25.160
We can't change this.

578
33:25.230 --> 33:27.430
Once we settle down,

579
33:27.920 --> 33:29.840
we'll get those shrapnel fragments

580
33:29.840 --> 33:30.920
out of you.

581
33:31.880 --> 33:33.540
Things that aren't part of you

582
33:34.550 --> 33:36.350
never truly fit.

583
33:36.790 --> 33:39.020
Just sticking to conservative treatment

584
33:39.020 --> 33:41.020
will only make the infection worse.

585
33:41.360 --> 33:45.320
Jiaxiang, you're not just talking about medicine, are you?

586
33:47.650 --> 33:48.650
Yes.

587
33:48.730 --> 33:51.860
This Politburo meeting was very successful,

588
33:53.680 --> 33:54.720
but I'm worried

589
33:55.270 --> 33:58.070
that the foreign advisor won't take it lying down.

590
33:58.070 --> 33:59.960
As long as he's still in that position,

591
33:59.960 --> 34:02.020
he'll cause trouble sooner or later.

592
34:04.250 --> 34:05.180
Comrade Zedong,

593
34:05.590 --> 34:07.250
what do you think we should do?

594
34:09.190 --> 34:10.120
To consolidate.

595
34:11.440 --> 34:12.949
First, we need to solidify the gains

596
34:12.949 --> 34:15.360
from this Politburo's resolution.

597
34:15.510 --> 34:16.429
How?

598
34:16.850 --> 34:18.780
What's the top priority right now?

599
34:21.630 --> 34:23.889
The top priority is helping you pass gas.

600
34:24.130 --> 34:24.940
Come on.

601
34:25.630 --> 34:27.960
Passing gas? How can that be the top priority?

602
34:27.960 --> 34:29.469
It is the top priority.

603
34:46.320 --> 34:47.239
You passed gas?

604
34:49.260 --> 34:50.260
He really did.

605
34:52.000 --> 34:52.850
You see,

606
34:53.190 --> 34:54.889
one more person, one more helping hand.

607
34:54.889 --> 34:56.020
Let's keep walking.

608
34:59.730 --> 35:01.190
Eight winds can't move me,

609
35:01.780 --> 35:03.440
one breath crosses the river.

610
35:09.550 --> 35:13.330
[Taoyuan County Town, Hunan]

611
35:09.760 --> 35:11.430
If the enemy grabs you by the neck...

612
35:11.430 --> 35:12.320
Come on,

613
35:12.760 --> 35:13.480
let's try.

614
35:14.960 --> 35:16.010
If he grabs you by the neck,

615
35:16.010 --> 35:17.190
you can fight back.

616
35:17.510 --> 35:19.170
Then you strike downward — go!

617
35:20.670 --> 35:21.840
Come on.

618
35:23.070 --> 35:23.880
Got it?

619
35:24.550 --> 35:26.150
Kuining, over here.

620
35:26.170 --> 35:27.500
Now, if the enemy wraps his arms around your waist...

621
35:27.500 --> 35:28.710
And he's stronger than you.

622
35:28.710 --> 35:29.670
What do you do?

623
35:30.230 --> 35:31.230
Hit him right here.

624
35:31.230 --> 35:32.490
That's the funny bone.

625
35:32.950 --> 35:33.440
Go.

626
35:35.450 --> 35:36.660
Come on, get up.

627
35:37.640 --> 35:37.940
Come on.

628
35:37.940 --> 35:38.870
Comrade He Long.

629
35:40.020 --> 35:40.950
Comrade He Long.

630
35:41.400 --> 35:42.230
Comrade He Long,

631
35:42.230 --> 35:43.510
the battle report's in.

632
35:43.510 --> 35:44.110
We wiped out

633
35:44.110 --> 35:44.730
Push harder!

634
35:44.730 --> 35:46.690
nearly 2 regiments

635
35:47.400 --> 35:49.200
of the 34th Independent Brigade

636
35:49.230 --> 35:50.540
and routed another one.

637
35:50.540 --> 35:53.390
We captured huge amounts of weapons, ammunition, and supplies.

638
35:53.180 --> 35:54.950
[Xiao Ke, Captain of the 6th Red Army Corps]

639
35:54.280 --> 35:55.070
What did I tell you?

640
35:55.070 --> 35:57.130
[Rudolf Alfred Bosshardt, Missionary]

641
35:55.440 --> 35:57.250
The 34th Independent Brigade was a fat piece of meat.

642
35:57.250 --> 35:58.980
We'd be fools not to take a bite.

643
35:59.320 --> 36:00.070
Push hard!

644
36:00.200 --> 36:01.400
We really stuck it

645
36:01.630 --> 36:03.070
to He Jian this time.

646
36:03.440 --> 36:04.550
We have to hurt them bad enough

647
36:04.550 --> 36:06.010
that they pull troops back

648
36:06.030 --> 36:08.550
to reinforce Changsha.

649
36:09.070 --> 36:10.960
If they don't reinforce Changsha,

650
36:10.960 --> 36:12.380
the pressure on our Central Red Army

651
36:12.380 --> 36:13.180
won't let up.

652
36:16.800 --> 36:17.510
Come on.

653
36:18.050 --> 36:19.090
Not bad, kid.

654
36:19.420 --> 36:20.500
Be careful.

655
36:20.640 --> 36:21.840
Again, again, again.

656
36:21.960 --> 36:23.150
No more, Commander.

657
36:23.510 --> 36:25.650
You've thrown me 8 times already this morning.

658
36:25.650 --> 36:27.380
I'm gonna see if lunch's ready.

659
36:29.050 --> 36:30.480
This is the medicine list

660
36:30.510 --> 36:32.230
Mr. Rudolf Alfred Bosshardt helped us verify.

661
36:32.230 --> 36:32.870
Great!

662
36:33.280 --> 36:34.320
Come here.

663
36:35.030 --> 36:36.280
This is really great.

664
36:36.360 --> 36:37.400
Comrade Bishi

665
36:37.820 --> 36:39.290
keeps telegraphing me saying

666
36:39.290 --> 36:42.560
we're short on medicine all across Hunan-Hubei-Sichuan-Guizhou.

667
36:42.560 --> 36:45.500
With this, he could open his own pharmacy.

668
36:48.380 --> 36:50.640
Thank you, Mr. Rudolf Alfred Bosshardt.

669
36:51.610 --> 36:52.610
It's my pleasure.

670
36:53.970 --> 36:54.850
But

671
36:55.940 --> 36:58.190
do you really intend to pay full price?

672
36:58.320 --> 36:59.190
Of course.

673
36:59.280 --> 37:01.340
But you're the occupying force here.

674
37:01.550 --> 37:02.710
And from what I know,

675
37:03.230 --> 37:04.960
you're not exactly wealthy.

676
37:06.150 --> 37:08.480
The Red Army has discipline.

677
37:09.460 --> 37:10.800
We don't take things without paying.

678
37:10.800 --> 37:12.040
If we did,

679
37:12.070 --> 37:14.130
what would make us any different from bandits?

680
37:14.130 --> 37:14.920
Besides,

681
37:15.020 --> 37:17.220
the people wouldn't support us either.

682
37:19.170 --> 37:21.040
God sends you here.

683
37:21.340 --> 37:22.220
No, no, no.

684
37:22.560 --> 37:23.890
We are sent by the Party,

685
37:24.150 --> 37:25.810
the Communist Party of China.

686
37:26.130 --> 37:30.290
The Communist Party of China.

687
37:32.610 --> 37:33.350
Report!

688
37:35.540 --> 37:39.670
An urgent telegram from the Central Revolutionary Military Commission.

689
37:44.420 --> 37:45.640
This is interesting.

690
37:46.070 --> 37:46.980
What does it say?

691
37:46.980 --> 37:48.170
The Military Commission has resolved

692
37:48.170 --> 37:50.230
for us to hold position around Changde

693
37:50.230 --> 37:51.670
and pin down the Hunan Army.

694
37:51.670 --> 37:53.630
If they pull forces back to reinforce,

695
37:53.630 --> 37:56.190
we will push west to Yongshun.

696
37:57.670 --> 37:59.730
The Central Red Army isn't coming to meet up with us?

697
37:59.730 --> 38:03.130
The Central Committee has decided to go to northern Guizhou.

698
38:03.620 --> 38:06.230
Looks like the central strategic direction has changed.

699
38:06.230 --> 38:07.480
What do we do?

700
38:08.880 --> 38:09.720
Obey orders.

701
38:09.920 --> 38:11.520
And stir up even more trouble

702
38:11.800 --> 38:13.240
in western Hunan.

703
38:13.880 --> 38:18.130
[Hunan Changsha]

704
38:14.400 --> 38:18.130
Commander-in-Chief, are you worried about He Long pushing south?

705
38:19.890 --> 38:23.080
If He Long takes Changde

706
38:23.250 --> 38:24.320
and crosses the Yuan River,

707
38:24.320 --> 38:26.360
he'll be a stone's throw from Changsha.

708
38:26.200 --> 38:28.020
[He Jian, Commander-in-Chief of the KMT "Pursuit Army"， Chairman of the Hunan Provincial Government]

709
38:26.670 --> 38:28.150
And all our troops

710
38:28.590 --> 38:32.670
are tied down in southwestern Hunan encircling Zhu and Mao's Communists.

711
38:32.670 --> 38:34.070
By the time we get back,

712
38:34.800 --> 38:37.550
it'll be too late.

713
38:38.570 --> 38:42.660
We'll be in big trouble.

714
38:43.890 --> 38:45.740
But if we pull back now,

715
38:45.770 --> 38:48.370
how will we explain it to the Generalissimo?

716
38:48.900 --> 38:50.130
Didn't he always say

717
38:50.270 --> 38:53.230
"act vigorously, quickly, and firmly"?

718
38:53.760 --> 38:55.110
What's to explain?

719
38:56.780 --> 38:58.440
Zhu and Mao going into Guizhou

720
38:58.590 --> 39:00.550
is Wang Jialie's problem.

721
39:04.070 --> 39:06.960
If He Long crosses the Yuan River,

722
39:07.650 --> 39:09.730
it will be my problem.

723
39:10.130 --> 39:12.130
When my life's on the line,

724
39:12.910 --> 39:14.720
I've got to look out for myself.

725
39:15.060 --> 39:17.520
You make a good point, Commander-in-Chief.

726
39:23.710 --> 39:27.380
I heard Xu Yuanquan in Hubei

727
39:27.620 --> 39:30.480
was worried about the Communists moving north too.

728
39:30.920 --> 39:34.360
He never obeyed the order to move into Sichuan.

729
39:34.920 --> 39:36.690
He kept all his main forces

730
39:36.710 --> 39:38.020
in western Hubei

731
39:38.210 --> 39:40.480
and western Hunan.

732
39:40.990 --> 39:45.330
And the Generalissimo never punished him for it.

733
39:45.920 --> 39:48.480
So all that

734
39:48.670 --> 39:50.870
"act vigorously, quickly, and firmly"

735
39:50.960 --> 39:52.480
talk is just a talk.

736
39:52.530 --> 39:54.060
Nobody takes it seriously.

737
39:54.460 --> 39:56.230
Then we'll do the same:

738
39:56.260 --> 40:00.260
when a general is in the field, he may disregard orders from the capital.

739
40:07.400 --> 40:09.020
Send a telegram to Huixian (Liu Jianxu).

740
40:09.020 --> 40:11.450
Tell him to immediately order the 19th Division,

741
40:11.450 --> 40:14.780
62nd Division and 16th Division to march north at full speed

742
40:14.920 --> 40:16.250
to reinforce Changsha.

743
40:16.320 --> 40:17.030
Yes, sir.

744
40:18.480 --> 40:19.740
Commander-in-Chief,

745
40:19.920 --> 40:22.250
what about the Generalissimo?

746
40:26.210 --> 40:28.100
Send a telegram to the Generalissimo.

747
40:28.100 --> 40:30.940
Choose your words carefully.

748
40:31.590 --> 40:34.910
Tell him Changde is in critical danger,

749
40:34.940 --> 40:38.540
and Changsha is also at risk of falling to the Communists.

750
40:38.970 --> 40:40.450
Pulling troops back

751
40:40.480 --> 40:43.520
is not only a desperate necessity,

752
40:43.690 --> 40:45.370
but also in line with the goal of

753
40:45.370 --> 40:47.570
"act vigorously, quickly, and firmly"

754
40:47.710 --> 40:49.920
to wipe out He Long and Xiao Ke's forces.

755
40:51.410 --> 40:55.220
Guizhou's turning into a Tang Monk's meat.

756
40:56.190 --> 40:58.110
Everyone wants a piece.

757
40:59.660 --> 41:01.500
I can't have it.

758
41:02.770 --> 41:04.730
I'm afraid it'd crack my teeth.

759
41:05.070 --> 41:09.710
Also, beg the Generalissimo to send reinforcements to Changde.

760
41:10.220 --> 41:13.620
Mark the telegram "URGENT".

761
41:14.460 --> 41:15.130
Yes, sir.

762
41:15.450 --> 41:18.530
[Nanchang Headquarters, Jiangxi]

763
41:18.530 --> 41:20.060
[Nanchang Headquarters, Jiangxi]

764
41:19.430 --> 41:20.430
Generalissimo,

765
41:21.150 --> 41:22.950
an urgent telegram from He Jian.

766
41:27.530 --> 41:29.150
[Yan Daogang, Director of the Attendants' Office of the Generalissimo of the Military Affairs Commission]

767
41:29.640 --> 41:31.110
He Jian

768
41:31.280 --> 41:33.640
is dead set on saving his own skin!

769
41:34.200 --> 41:36.260
The situation in Changde really is critical.

770
41:36.260 --> 41:38.920
He knows I can't do anything about him right now.

771
41:39.420 --> 41:40.550
Where's Xue Boling (Xue Yue)?

772
41:40.550 --> 41:42.920
His vanguard has already reached Zhenyuan.

773
41:42.920 --> 41:45.290
Tell Xue Boling: the top priority

774
41:45.590 --> 41:48.000
for this Guizhou campaign is taking Guiyang.

775
41:48.000 --> 41:50.550
Tell him to guard his own plate of meat

776
41:50.960 --> 41:52.480
so that the wolves won't come sniffing,

777
41:52.480 --> 41:54.000
especially that Guangxi wolf!

778
41:54.000 --> 41:54.550
Yes, sir.

779
41:54.710 --> 41:56.640
I'll send the telegram to Commander Xue right away

780
41:56.640 --> 41:58.350
and explain the stakes.

781
42:03.300 --> 42:04.700
Has He Guoguang arrived?

782
42:05.050 --> 42:05.740
He has.

783
42:06.510 --> 42:07.230
Send him in.

784
42:07.320 --> 42:07.850
Yes, sir.

785
42:17.680 --> 42:18.530
Brother Yuanjing.

786
42:18.530 --> 42:19.380
Greetings, Generalissimo.

787
42:19.380 --> 42:21.110
Brother Yuanjing, please sit.

788
42:21.560 --> 42:22.650
[He Guoguang, Director of the 1st Department, Nanchang Headquarters]

789
42:26.930 --> 42:28.260
I'll help myself.

790
42:28.510 --> 42:29.510
Sit down, please.

791
42:29.560 --> 42:30.640
Don't get up. Sit.

792
42:31.520 --> 42:32.580
Please take a seat.

793
42:45.960 --> 42:46.730
Have a taste.

794
42:59.230 --> 43:00.760
How is it?

795
43:01.920 --> 43:02.550
Fragrant.
